rId}** - fulfilment.status | ✓ COMPUTED | OrderController compares allocated/delivered against order quantity |\n  | **GET /orders** - pagination | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | Supports limit (1-100, default 100) and offset (>=0, default 0) with X-Total-Count |\n  | **GET /orders** - fulfilment filter | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | ?fulfilment=STATUS filters list before pagination; validates status value (HTTP 400 on invalid) |\n  | **GET /shipments** - pagination | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | Supports limit (1-100, default 100) and offset (>=0, default 0) with X-Total-Count |\n  | **POST /orders** - quantity validation | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | Rejects quantity < 1 with HTTP 400 naming field; defaults to 1 if not provided |\n  | **POST /orders** - customer validation | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | Rejects non-existent customer with HTTP 422 (UnprocessableEntityException) through error envelope |\n  | **POST /shipments** - quantity validation | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | Rejects quantity < 1 with HTTP 400; defaults to 1 if not provided |\n  | **POST /shipments** - allocation validation | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | Sums non-CANCELLED shipments via repository.findByOrderId(); rejects allocation exceeding order.quantity with HTTP 409 |\n  | **POST /shipments/{id}/confirm** | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | Transitions CREATED→CONFIRMED; rejects other states with HTTP 409 |\n  | **POST /shipments/{id}/deliver** | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | Transitions CONFIRMED→DELIVERED; rejects other states with HTTP 409 |\n  | **POST /shipments/{id}/cancel** | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | Transitions CREATED→CANCELLED; rejects other states with HTTP 409 |\n  | **PUT /orders/{id}/quantity** | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | Sets quantity if >= allocated; rejects below allocated with HTTP 409; validates >= 1 with HTTP 400 |\n  \n  ## Tests Covering New Features\n  \n  **OrderControllerTest (16 tests):**\n  - quantity default of 1\n  - custom quantity creation\n  - quantity < 1 rejection\n  - non-existent customer rejection (HTTP 422)\n  - pagination limit/offset\n  - pagination X-Total-Count header\n  - pagination invalid limit\n  - pagination negative offset\n  - fulfilment filter (UNALLOCATED)\n  - fulfilment filter invalid status\n  - order quantity amendment\n  - amendment rejection when below allocated\n  - Plus 4 baseline tests (create, read, 404, duplicate)\n  \n  **ShipmentControllerTest (15 tests):**\n  - quantity default of 1\n  - custom quantity creation\n  - quantity < 1 rejection\n  - confirm transition (CREATED→CONFIRMED)\n  - deliver transition (CONFIRMED→DELIVERED)\n  - cancel transition (CREATED→CANCELLED)\n  - invalid transition rejection\n  - allocation validation preventing exceed\n  - cancelled shipment releasing quantity\n  - pagination with X-Total-Count\n  - Plus 5 baseline tests (create, duplicate, read, 404, list ordering)\n  \n  **CustomerControllerTest (6 tests):**\n  - 404 error envelope verification\n  - pagination with limit/offset\n  - pagination X-Total-Count header\n  - pagination invalid limit\n  - pagination negative offset\n  - Plus 1 baseline test (create)\n  \n  ## Verification\n  \n  ```\n  BUILD SUCCESS\n  Tests run: 38, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\n  ```\n  \n  All existing tests pass (baseline behavior preserved), and all new tests for the three features pass. No new Maven dependencies added. No files modified outside order, shipment, customer, and api packages except tests.\nagentId: aad07ef734d9894ba (use SendMessage with to: 'aad07ef734d9894ba', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 65200\ntool_uses: 39\nduration_ms: 285061</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3757ef9-0b0c-45f0-806d-82d20c07e534","uuid":"4ae38643-faf7-4c1e-bf41-e808ada59ca0","timestamp":"2026-09-25T09:04:47.038Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"BE-005 — Partial fulfilment, customer check, paged lists\n\nThree changes to `sample-service`, shipped together on one branch. They touch the order,\nshipment and customer features and the shared `api` package.\n\n## 1. Partial fulfilment\n\nAn order is for a quantity of goods, and that quantity is shipped in parts. Today an order\nhas no quantity, a shipment carries no quantity, and nothing records how much of an order\nits shipments account for.\n\n- An order gains a `quantity`: a positive integer, `1` when the request does not give one.\n  A quantity below `1` is rejected with HTTP 400 naming the field. `GET /orders/{orderId}`\n  reports it.\n- A shipment gains a `quantity` with the same rule and the same default.\n- An order's shipments **allocate** its quantity. `POST /shipments` is rejected with HTTP 409,\n  and nothing changes, when the shipment would push the order's allocated quantity above the\n  order's quantity. The allocated quantity is the sum over the order's shipments that are not\n  `CANCELLED`. Creating a shipment for an order that does not exist keeps its current\n  behaviour.\n- Shipments gain transitions: `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` moves `CREATED` to\n  `CONFIRMED`; `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/deliver` moves `CONFIRMED` to `DELIVERED`, a new\n  status; `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/cancel` moves `CREATED` to `CANCELLED`. Each returns\n  the shipment. Any other transition is rejected with HTTP 409 and changes nothing; an\n  unknown shipment is rejected with HTTP 404.\n- An order gains a fulfilment status, reported by `GET /orders/{orderId}` and by the list as\n  `fulfilment: { allocated, delivered, status }`. A newly created order is `UNALLOCATED`.\n  `delivered` is the sum over the order's `DELIVERED` shipments. The status is `DELIVERED`\n  when `delivered` reaches the order's quantity, `FULLY_ALLOCATED` when `allocated` reaches\n  it, `PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED` when `allocated` is above zero and below it, and `UNALLOCATED`\n  otherwise.\n- `GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS` lists only the orders in that status. Without the parameter\n  the list is unchanged. A value that is not a fulfilment status is rejected with HTTP 400\n  naming the parameter.\n- **Cancelling a shipment releases its quantity.** After the cancel, the order's fulfilment no\n  longer counts that shipment, its status moves back accordingly, and a new shipment for the\n  released quantity is accepted.\n- **An order's quantity can be amended after shipments exist.** `PUT /orders/{orderId}/quantity`\n  with `{ \"quantity\": n }` sets it, under the same positive-integer rule (HTTP 400 naming the\n  field); an unknown order is HTTP 404. The amendment is rejected with HTTP 409, and nothing\n  changes, when the new quantity is below the order's allocated quantity. After an amendment the\n  order's fulfilment reflects the new quantity: an order that was `FULLY_ALLOCATED` at 4 is\n  `PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED` at 6, and its shipments then allocate against 6.\n\n## 2. An order needs its customer\n\nToday `POST /orders` accepts any `customerId`. From now on an order for a customer that does\nnot exist is rejected with HTTP 422 through the error envelope. `GET /customers/{customerId}`\nfor an unknown customer reports HTTP 404 **through the error envelope**, like orders and\nshipments already do.\n\nThe existing `OrderControllerTest` creates orders for a customer that was never created.\nUpdate it so that the suite reflects the new rule.\n\n## 3. Paged lists\n\n`GET /customers`, `GET /orders` and `GET /shipments` accept `limit` (1 to 100, default 100)\nand `offset` (0 or more, default 0), and slice the list in id order. The response body stays\nthe array it is today, so callers that do not page keep working, and every list response\ncarries the total number of items before slicing in an `X-Total-Count` header. A `limit`\noutside its range or a negative `offset` is rejected with HTTP 400 naming the parameter. On\n`GET /orders` the total is the total after the `fulfilment` filter.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- The existing Kotlin + Spring Boot architecture must be preserved.\n- Do not add new dependencies.\n- Do not modify files outside the order, shipment and customer features and the shared `api`\n  package, except tests.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Existing build passes.\n2. Existing tests pass, other than `OrderControllerTest`, which this ticket changes.\n3. Quantities, allocation, the three transitions, the fulfilment read model and the filter\n   behave as specified, including the release of a cancelled shipment's quantity and the\n   amendment of an order's quantity.\n4. Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API.\n5. An order for an unknown customer is refused; every list pages as specified and unpaged\n   calls are unchanged.\n6. No new Maven dependency appears.\n7. No unrelated production file changes.\n\n---\n\nPLANNER'S HANDOFF:\n\n## Read Paths Analysis\n\n| Path | Value | Stored or Computed | Where Computed |\n|------|-------|-------------------|-----------------|\n| **GET /customers** (query: limit, offset) | customerId | STORED | InMemoryCustomerRepository |\n| | name | STORED | InMemoryCustomerRepository |\n| | email | STORED | InMemoryCustomerRepository |\n| | X-Total-Count header | COMPUTED | CustomerController (count all customers) |\n| | Array ordering | STORED | InMemoryCustomerRepository.findAll() sorts by customerId |\n| **GET /customers/{customerId}** | customerId | STORED | InMemoryCustomerRepository.findById() |\n| | name | STORED | InMemoryCustomerRepository.findById() |\n| | email | STORED | InMemoryCustomerRepository.findById() |\n| **GET /orders/{orderId}** | orderId | STORED | InMemoryOrderRepository |\n| | customerId | STORED | InMemoryOrderRepository |\n| | amount | STORED | InMemoryOrderRepository |\n| | currency | STORED | InMemoryOrderRepository |\n| | quantity | STORED | Order entity (default 1 if not provided) |\n| | fulfilment.allocated | COMPUTED | OrderController aggregates non-CANCELLED shipments' quantities via shipment repository |\n| | fulfilment.delivered | COMPUTED | OrderController aggregates DELIVERED shipments' quantities via shipment repository |\n| | fulfilment.status | COMPUTED | OrderController compares allocated/delivered against order quantity |\n| **GET /orders** (query: limit, offset, fulfilment) | (array of above fields) | STORED/COMPUTED | As above |\n| | X-Total-Count header | COMPUTED | OrderController counts orders matching fulfilment filter before applying pagination |\n| | Array ordering | STORED | InMemoryOrderRepository.findAll() sorts by orderId |\n| **GET /shipments/{shipmentId}** | shipmentId | STORED | InMemoryShipmentRepository |\n| | orderId | STORED | InMemoryShipmentRepository |\n| | carrier | STORED | InMemoryShipmentRepository |\n| | quantity | STORED | Shipment entity (default 1 if not provided) |\n| | status | STORED | Shipment entity (CREATED, CONFIRMED, DELIVERED, CANCELLED) |\n| **GET /shipments** (query: limit, offset) | (array of above fields) | STORED | As above |\n| | X-Total-Count header | COMPUTED | ShipmentController counts all shipments |\n| | Array ordering | STORED | InMemoryShipmentRepository.findAll() sorts by shipmentId |\n| **POST /orders** (body: quantity optional) | (same as GET /orders/{orderId}) | STORED/COMPUTED | OrderController: validates quantity positive, checks customer exists, returns created order with computed fulfilment |\n| **POST /shipments** (body: quantity optional) | (same as GET /shipments/{shipmentId}) | STORED/COMPUTED | ShipmentController: validates quantity positive, checks allocation does not exceed order quantity (computed via shipment repository sum), returns created shipment |\n| **PUT /orders/{orderId}/quantity** (body: quantity) | (same as GET /orders/{orderId}) | STORED/COMPUTED | OrderController: validates quantity positive, rejects if below current allocation, returns updated order with recalculated fulfilment |\n| **POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm** | (same as GET /shipments/{shipmentId}) | STORED | ShipmentController transitions status CREATED → CONFIRMED, returns shipment |\n| **POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/deliver** | (same as GET /shipments/{shipmentId}) | STORED | ShipmentController transitions status CONFIRMED → DELIVERED, returns shipment |\n| **POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/cancel** | (same as GET /shipments/{shipmentId}) | STORED | ShipmentController transitions status CREATED → CANCELLED, returns shipment |\n| **POST /customers** (body: customerId, name, email) | customerId, name, email | STORED | InMemoryCustomerRepository.save() |\n\n## Shape\n\nAll list endpoints (GET /customers, GET /orders, GET /shipments) return arrays of entities sorted by ID, with pagination controlled by `limit` (1-100, default 100) and `offset` (0 or more, default 0) query parameters, and report the total pre-filtered, pre-paginated count in an `X-Total-Count` response header. Single-entity reads return the entity with all fields. Order fulfilment status and allocated/delivered quantities are computed at read time by aggregating across the shipment repository for that order. Shipment allocation validation at creation time sums existing non-cancelled shipment quantities for the target order via the repository.\n\n## Unresolved\n\n1. **Customer existence validation on order creation (HTTP 422)**: The ticket specifies orders for non-existent customers are rejected with HTTP 422 \"through the error envelope,\" but ApiExceptions.kt only defines ResourceNotFoundException (404), ConflictException (409), and ValidationException (400). An `UnprocessableEntityException` class returning HTTP 422 is not present in the codebase and would need to be added to the api package.\n\n2. **Shipment-to-Order lookup for allocation validation**: The ShipmentRepository provides `findAll()` sorted by ID, but lacks a method to query shipments by orderId. The POST /shipments validation logic requires summing quantities of non-cancelled shipments for a specific order; the repository helper method to perform this lookup is unresolved.\n\n3. **Error envelope for GET /customers/{customerId}**: The current CustomerController returns HTTP 404 via `ResponseEntity.notFound().build()` (line 28), which bypasses the GlobalExceptionHandler and error envelope. The ticket requires it to report 404 \"through the error envelope\" like orders and shipments, implying a ResourceNotFoundException should be thrown instead. The implementation pattern change is unresolved.\n\n4. **X-Total-Count computation with fulfilment filter**: The list endpoint must report the count after applying the fulfilment filter but before pagination. Whether this count is computed inline in the controller or via a repository method is unresolved from the baseline.","agentId":"aad07ef734d9894ba","agentType":"implementer","harnessNoteCount":0,"harnessTailCount":0,"harnessSectionHash":"ce1e1153f10e4322","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All 38 tests pass. Here is the implementation handoff:\n\n## Changed\n\n**Production code files:**\n\n1. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-a390a301-eb67-45a5-b22d-d6e43a922e85/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt` - Added `UnprocessableEntityException` for HTTP 422 responses required for customer validation on order creation\n\n2. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-a390a301-eb67-45a5-b22d-d6e43a922e85/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt` - Added error codes: `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND`, `CUSTOMER_DOES_NOT_EXIST`, `INVALID_QUANTITY`, `ALLOCATION_CONFLICT`, `INVALID_TRANSITION`\n\n3. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-a390a301-eb67-45a5-b22d-d6e43a922e85/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/Order.kt` - Added `quantity: Int` field, `OrderFulfilment` data class with `allocated`, `delivered`, `status` fields, `FulfilmentStatus` enum (UNALLOCATED, PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED, FULLY_ALLOCATED, DELIVERED), and `UpdateOrderQuantityRequest` for amendment endpoint\n\n4. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-a390a301-eb67-45a5-b22d-d6e43a922e85/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderController.kt` - Complete rewrite to add: quantity validation (>=1, HTTP 400), customer existence check (HTTP 422), fulfilment computation from shipment repository, pagination support (limit 1-100, offset >=0), `fulfilment` query filter, `PUT /orders/{orderId}/quantity` amendment endpoint with allocation conflict checking\n\n5. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-a390a301-eb67-45a5-b22d-d6e43a922e85/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt` - Added `quantity: Int` field and `DELIVERED` status to `ShipmentStatus` enum\n\n6. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-a390a301-eb67-45a5-b22d-d6e43a922e85/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt` - Added `findByOrderId(orderId: String)` method to support allocation validation and fulfilment computation\n\n7. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-a390a301-eb67-45a5-b22d-d6e43a922e85/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt` - Added quantity validation (>=1, HTTP 400), allocation validation (HTTP 409 when exceeding order quantity), `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` (CREATED→CONFIRMED), `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/deliver` (CONFIRMED→DELIVERED), `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/cancel` (CREATED→CANCELLED), pagination support with X-Total-Count header\n\n8. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-a390a301-eb67-45a5-b22d-d6e43a922e85/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/CustomerController.kt` - Changed 404 handling from `ResponseEntity.notFound()` to throw `ResourceNotFoundException` to use error envelope, added pagination support (limit 1-100, offset >=0) with X-Total-Count header\n\n**Test files:**\n\n9. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-a390a301-eb67-45a5-b22d-d6e43a922e85/sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderControllerTest.kt` - Updated to create customer in setup; added 12 new tests covering quantity defaults, validation, customer existence, pagination, fulfilment filter, and amendment\n\n10. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-a390a301-eb67-45a5-b22d-d6e43a922e85/sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Updated to create customer and order in setup; added 10 new tests covering quantity, transitions (confirm/deliver/cancel), allocation validation, quantity release on cancel, and pagination\n\n11. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-a390a301-eb67-45a5-b22d-d6e43a922e85/sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/CustomerControllerTest.kt` - Updated 404 test to verify error envelope; added 3 new tests for pagination with limit/offset validation\n\n## Against Plan's Read-Path Table\n\n| Path | Implemented | Notes |\n|------|-------------|-------|\n| **GET /customers** - pagination (limit, offset) | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | Response body is array in id order; X-Total-Count header added via ResponseEntity.header() |\n| **GET /customers** - X-Total-Count | ✓ STORED→COMPUTED | CustomerController computes total count of all customers |\n| **GET /customers/{customerId}** - error envelope | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | Now throws ResourceNotFoundException instead of ResponseEntity.notFound() |\n| **GET /orders/{orderId}** - quantity | ✓ STORED | Order entity has quantity field, default 1 when not provided |\n| **GET /orders/{orderId}** - fulfilment.allocated | ✓ COMPUTED | OrderController.computeFulfilment() sums non-CANCELLED shipments via repository.findByOrderId() |\n| **GET /orders/{orderId}** - fulfilment.delivered | ✓ COMPUTED | OrderController.computeFulfilment() sums DELIVERED shipments via repository.findByOrderId() |\n| **GET /orders/{orderId}** - fulfilment.status | ✓ COMPUTED | OrderController compares allocated/delivered against order quantity |\n| **GET /orders** - pagination | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | Supports limit (1-100, default 100) and offset (>=0, default 0) with X-Total-Count |\n| **GET /orders** - fulfilment filter | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | ?fulfilment=STATUS filters list before pagination; validates status value (HTTP 400 on invalid) |\n| **GET /shipments** - pagination | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | Supports limit (1-100, default 100) and offset (>=0, default 0) with X-Total-Count |\n| **POST /orders** - quantity validation | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | Rejects quantity < 1 with HTTP 400 naming field; defaults to 1 if not provided |\n| **POST /orders** - customer validation | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | Rejects non-existent customer with HTTP 422 (UnprocessableEntityException) through error envelope |\n| **POST /shipments** - quantity validation | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | Rejects quantity < 1 with HTTP 400; defaults to 1 if not provided |\n| **POST /shipments** - allocation validation | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | Sums non-CANCELLED shipments via repository.findByOrderId(); rejects allocation exceeding order.quantity with HTTP 409 |\n| **POST /shipments/{id}/confirm** | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | Transitions CREATED→CONFIRMED; rejects other states with HTTP 409 |\n| **POST /shipments/{id}/deliver** | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | Transitions CONFIRMED→DELIVERED; rejects other states with HTTP 409 |\n| **POST /shipments/{id}/cancel** | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | Transitions CREATED→CANCELLED; rejects other states with HTTP 409 |\n| **PUT /orders/{id}/quantity** | ✓ IMPLEMENTED | Sets quantity if >= allocated; rejects below allocated with HTTP 409; validates >= 1 with HTTP 400 |\n\n## Tests Covering New Features\n\n**OrderControllerTest (16 tests):**\n- quantity default of 1\n- custom quantity creation\n- quantity < 1 rejection\n- non-existent customer rejection (HTTP 422)\n- pagination limit/offset\n- pagination X-Total-Count header\n- pagination invalid limit\n- pagination negative offset\n- fulfilment filter (UNALLOCATED)\n- fulfilment filter invalid status\n- order quantity amendment\n- amendment rejection when below allocated\n- Plus 4 baseline tests (create, read, 404, duplicate)\n\n**ShipmentControllerTest (15 tests):**\n- quantity default of 1\n- custom quantity creation\n- quantity < 1 rejection\n- confirm transition (CREATED→CONFIRMED)\n- deliver transition (CONFIRMED→DELIVERED)\n- cancel transition (CREATED→CANCELLED)\n- invalid transition rejection\n- allocation validation preventing exceed\n- cancelled shipment releasing quantity\n- pagination with X-Total-Count\n- Plus 5 baseline tests (create, duplicate, read, 404, list ordering)\n\n**CustomerControllerTest (6 tests):**\n- 404 error envelope verification\n- pagination with limit/offset\n- pagination X-Total-Count header\n- pagination invalid limit\n- pagination negative offset\n- Plus 1 baseline test (create)\n\n## Verification\n\n```\nBUILD SUCCESS\nTests run: 38, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\n```\n\nAll existing tests pass (baseline behavior preserved), and all new tests for the three features pass. No new Maven dependencies added. No files modified outside order, shipment, customer, and api packages except tests."}],"resolvedModel":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","totalDurationMs":285061,"totalTokens":65200,"totalToolUseCount":39,"usage":{"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":31},"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1950,"cache_read_input_tokens":60529,"output_tokens":2713,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1950},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":8,"output_tokens":2713,"cache_read_input_tokens":60529,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1950,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1950,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":19,"searchCount":0